2026-09-23 00:00:49,093 | INFO | [congress-pelosi-v4] [agents] name=bear mode=backtesting model=gemini-3.5-flash-lite cache_hit=False tokens_in=37940 tokens_out=833 tokens_cached_in=32302 tokens_uncached_in=5638 tokens_thinking=0 tokens_total=38773 latency_ms=4745 first_event_latency_ms=2169 tool_calls=1 observability_warnings=0 summary='### Bear Case Against Copying the Visible Book (As of 2026-01-23)  1. **Future Filing Violations & Look-Ahead Bias**:     Per the clock rule and research evidence, filings **20034836** (signed June 23, 2026) and **20035143** (signed August 21, 2026) carry signature dates strictly in the future relative to our simulation date of **2026-01-23**. Utilizing them would introduce severe look-ahead bias. Even the sole valid filing, **20033725**, is signed on January 23, 2026, meaning public availability lags actual execution and introduces significant timing risk.  2. **Broad Disclosure Ranges & Ambiguous Sizing**:     Congressional Periodic Transaction Reports (PTRs) only disclose broad transaction brackets (e.g., $15,001–$50,000, $1M–$5M) rather than exact share quantities or cost bases. Attempting to scale midpoints (across active names like GOOGL, AMZN, NVDA, VST, DIS, PYPL, TEM, and AB) to account value introduces arbitrary sizing errors that do not reflect true risk parameters.  3. **Execution Friction, Slippage, and Front-Running**:     Publicly disclosed trades are heavily scrutinized by market participants. Copycat trading creates clustered retail flow that can easily be front-run, resulting in wide bid-ask spreads, poor fill prices, and immediate negative slippage upon entry.  4. **Lack of Continuous Position Management**:     Disclosures reveal static point-in-time transactions without ongoing transparency into hedging strategies, option overlays, or subsequent exits. Blindly mimicking entries without visibility into management leaves copycat portfolios exposed to unmanaged drawdowns.  RESULT: Argued the comprehensive bear case against copying the visible book, detailing future filing disqualifications, range ambiguities, execution friction, and lack of ongoing management transparency, with no orders submitted.' trace=/Users/robertgrzesik/Library/Caches/lumibot/1.0/agent_runtime/traces/bear/f26708d40c808c4502c760fe3d4fc5ade77db15ad6749fdeb2040fdd53e11da7-20260923040049055996.json
