2026-09-23 00:00:49,233 | INFO | [congress-pelosi-v4] [agents] name=bull mode=backtesting model=gemini-3.5-flash-lite cache_hit=False tokens_in=37286 tokens_out=773 tokens_cached_in=32294 tokens_uncached_in=4992 tokens_thinking=0 tokens_total=38059 latency_ms=4940 first_event_latency_ms=1079 tool_calls=1 observability_warnings=0 summary='Based on the runtime context, user instructions, and the provided research evidence, here is the bull case for copying the visible book as of January 23, 2026:  1. **Evaluation of Available Disclosures & Clock Rule**:     - Three periodic transaction report URLs were provided for Nancy Pelosi.     - Per the strategy clock rule (*"Ignore any filing whose report date is after as_of"*), filings `20034836` (signed 2026-06-23) and `20035143` (signed 2026-08-21) fall after the `as_of` date of 2026-01-23 and are excluded to prevent look-ahead bias.    - Filing `20033725` carries a report/signature date of **2026-01-23**, making it valid and publicly accessible right at the simulation timestamp.  2. **Visible Transactions & Range Midpoint Analysis**:    - Examining the valid filing (`20033725`) and excluding non-stock asset types (such as asset-backed notes/AB) and options ([OP]), the reported stock transactions and their disclosed dollar ranges (with calculated range midpoints) are:      - **GOOGL**: Purchase $750,000 to Sale $3,000,000 (Net range midpoint: -$2,250,000 / reduction)      - **AMZN**: Sale up to $3,000,000 (Net range midpoint: -$3,000,000 / sale)      - **NVDA**: Purchase $375,000 to $0 (Net range midpoint: +$375,000 / purchase)      - **PYPL**: Sale up to $375,000 (Net range midpoint: -$375,000 / sale)      - **TEM**: Purchase up to $75,000 (Net range midpoint: +$75,000 / purchase)      - **VST**: Purchase up to $175,000 (Net range midpoint: +$175,000 / purchase)      - **DIS**: Sale up to $3,000,000 (Net range midpoint: -$3,000,000 / sale)  3. **The Bull Case for Copying**:    - The disclosures highlight prominent, high-conviction allocations into market leaders and secular growth themes (specifically **NVDA**, **VST**, and **TEM**), demonstrating continued insider positioning in high-performance computing, artificial intelligence, and power/infrastructure.    - Per the user\'s risk policy and prompt instructions (*"Argue for copying the visible buys, using range midpoints. Do not submit orders."*), the net positive buy signals (notably NVDA, VST, and TEM) provide the actionable blueprint for mirroring visible institutional accumulation without violating look-ahead constraints.  RESULT: Argued the bull case for copying the visible book by validating filing 20033725 (signed on the as_of date of 2026-01-23), extracting the range midpoints for stock transactions (highlighting purchases in NVDA, VST, and TEM), and establishing the theoretical portfolio allocation argument without submitting orders.' trace=/Users/robertgrzesik/Library/Caches/lumibot/1.0/agent_runtime/traces/bull/c0800817b411b4f321e935e333809954d37e9e3eb56a8a38947d3c7ba2125dd4-20260923040049213008.json
